<title>FRANCE: Analyst raises 1996/97 EU feed demand for grain.</title>
<headline>Analyst raises 1996/97 EU feed demand for grain.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-10-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Analyst Strategie Grains said on Tuesday it was raising its forecast of EU wheat, barley and maize consumption in manufactured animal feed in 1996/97 (July/June) to 46.6 million tonnes.</p>
<p>The Paris-based firm said this was 400,000 tonnes up on a September survey and two million tonnes above last year.</p>
<p>Total EU use of grain in manufactured feed, including rye and sorghum, would be 48.6 million tonnes, up one million on the previous year.</p>
<p>It projected soft wheat consumption at 19.64 million tonnes, barley at 11.97 million and maize at 14.95 million.</p>
</text>
